soul-alan-kay : List Word
soul-alan-kay = "Alan Kay (living, 86; still gives talks, among them UCLA CS 201 and the Kristen Nygaard centenary in 2026; long known for answering questions in public forums). Smalltalk, objects as messaging, the Dynabook for children, Viewpoints Research's STEPS (personal computing in about 20,000 lines). Relevance: hyperactivity is the smallest code completing the whole task, local-first software for every device, and education built into every interaction; STEPS is its precedent in volume and the Dynabook in purpose."
